{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789218622,"nonce":"SFNLFBfPujVT9wUdzE4SXgIxUiw=","title":"Pool free masked a small address to null and read it","message":"Segregated storage finds a block's slab by masking its address to the\nslab size, so every address below one slab masks to zero and reading a\nheader there is a null dereference. Found by a miscompiled program\npassing a non-pointer to free. Fixed: an address below SLAB is refused\nbefore anything reads through it, debug_assert loud, release quiet.","files":null}]}